# Files consumed by container builds must keep LF on every platform.
#
# Without this, a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true rewrites
# entrypoint.sh to CRLF. The kernel then reads the shebang as
# "/usr/bin/env bash\r" and looks for a binary literally named "bash\r",
# so every Linux runner container dies with exit code 127 before it can
# register, and queued jobs hang forever.
*.sh            text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
*.Dockerfile    text eol=lf
